config ZMK_BLE_SHELL_ADV_BEHAVIOR
    bool "BLE shell advertise behavior"
    depends on ZMK_BLE_SHELL
    help
      Adds the zmk,behavior-ble-shell-adv ZMK behavior.  When triggered
      from a keymap binding it starts a connectable legacy advertising
      session that broadcasts the shell GATT service UUID.  This allows a
      management UI client to discover and connect to the device.
      Advertising stops automatically after ZMK_BLE_SHELL_ADV_TIMEOUT
      seconds if no client subscribes to the shell characteristic.
      Requires BT_MAX_CONN > 1 to accept the second connection.

config ZMK_BLE_SHELL_ADV_TIMEOUT
    int "MUI advertisement timeout (seconds)"
    depends on ZMK_BLE_SHELL_ADV_BEHAVIOR
    default 30
    help
      How many seconds to advertise the shell service before giving up
      when no management UI client subscribes.
